window.COURSE = {"sections":[{"id":"overview","label":"Start Here","title":"🔴 Jeffrey's YouTube Bootcamp","group":"Start","groupEmoji":"🏁","emoji":"🔴","blurb":"What the job actually is, and your five 20-minute steps.","kind":"doc","quiz":null,"html":"<p><strong>You want to be a YouTuber. A real one.</strong> Not \"one day\" — starting now, at 12,\nwith the games and music you already love.</p>\n<p>Good news: some of the biggest gaming channels on Earth started exactly like this —\none kid, one game, one bad microphone. Bad news: most people quit at video three.\nThis course shows you how to be the one who doesn't.</p>\n<p>It takes <strong>20 minutes</strong>. It's serious — and it's meant to be fun.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>⏱️ Your 20 minutes</h2>\n<div id=\"paceTimer\"></div>\n\n<hr />\n<h2>🧭 What you'll walk away with</h2>\n<p>By the end you'll have:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>✅ A <strong>channel plan</strong> (your niche, your name, your first 10 videos)</li>\n<li>✅ A <strong>script formula</strong> for videos people actually finish</li>\n<li>✅ The <strong>upload checklist</strong> (title + thumbnail + description)</li>\n<li>✅ The <strong>growth rules</strong> the algorithm actually rewards</li>\n<li>✅ The <strong>safety rules</strong> every young creator needs</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<h2>🎮 Your unfair advantage</h2>\n<p>You already have what most beginners don't:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>You already have</th>\n<th>Why it matters</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Roblox + Rivals</strong> hours</td>\n<td>You know the game better than a casual viewer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>K-pop knowledge</strong></td>\n<td>Fandoms are the most engaged audiences on YouTube</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>You watch YouTubers</strong></td>\n<td>You already know what a good video feels like</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The plan: <strong>turn what you already do into content.</strong></p>\n<hr />\n<h2>🔥 The five steps</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>🔍 <strong>Understand the job</strong> — what a YouTuber actually <em>is</em></li>\n<li>🗺️ <strong>Plan your channel</strong> — niche, name, first 10 videos</li>\n<li>🎬 <strong>Make your first video</strong> — the script formula</li>\n<li>🚀 <strong>Upload like a pro</strong> — titles, thumbnails, timing</li>\n<li>📈 <strong>Grow &amp; stay safe</strong> — the rules that compound</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Each step has a quiz. Get them all and you've graduated Bootcamp. 🎖️</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>⚠️ One rule before we start</h2>\n<p><strong>Your parents know about your channel.</strong> Not \"they'll find out later\" — they know\nfrom video one. You'll see why in Step 5. It's not a fun rule. It's the one that\nprotects everything else.</p>\n<p>👇 <strong>Press Start on the timer. Let's go.</strong></p>"},{"id":"dashboard","label":"My Progress","title":"My Progress","group":"Start","groupEmoji":"🏁","emoji":"📈","blurb":"Your stars and quiz scores - saved in this browser.","kind":"dashboard","quiz":null,"html":""},{"id":"step-01","label":"1. Understand the Job","title":"🔍 Step 1: Understand the Job","group":"The 20 Minutes","groupEmoji":"⏱️","emoji":"🔍","blurb":"What a YouTuber really is - and why most channels quit.","kind":"doc","quiz":{"title":"Step 1 — Understand the Job","questions":[{"q":"What is a YouTuber's actual job, in one line?","options":["Make videos people choose to watch again and again","Get famous fast","Play games all day","Buy the best camera"],"answer":0,"why":"Everything else — money, fans, sponsors — is a result of that one sentence."},{"q":"What does the algorithm reward FIRST?","options":["Talent","Consistency","Expensive gear","Luck"],"answer":1,"why":"Reliability first. One video a week for months beats ten videos then silence."},{"q":"Most channels die at which video?","options":["Video 3","Video 100","Video 50","They never die"],"answer":0,"why":"Most people quit around video three. Not quitting is the whole trick."},{"q":"Which niche is stronger for starting?","options":["Gaming videos in general","Rivals loadout guides","Everything: gaming, vlogs, cooking","Whatever is trending that day"],"answer":1,"why":"Narrow beats broad. A few hundred competitors, not 50 million."}]},"html":"<p><strong>⏱️ 0:00 → 2:00 (2 minutes)</strong></p>\n<h2>🎯 Goal</h2>\n<p>Know what the job <em>actually</em> is — so you don't quit at video three like everyone else.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>🧠 What a YouTuber actually is</h2>\n<p>Forget the mansion tours. A YouTuber is:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Someone who makes videos people choose to watch — again and again.</strong></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>That's the whole job. Everything else (money, sponsors, fans) is a <em>result</em> of that\none sentence.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>🧠 The three jobs inside the job</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Job</th>\n<th>What it looks like</th>\n<th>Time it takes</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Creator</strong> 🎬</td>\n<td>Ideas, scripts, recording, editing</td>\n<td>~80%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Publisher</strong> 📤</td>\n<td>Titles, thumbnails, upload, timing</td>\n<td>~15%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Community</strong> 💬</td>\n<td>Comments, replies, discord</td>\n<td>~5% but it's everything</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Notice: <strong>editing is most of the work.</strong> If you only enjoy <em>playing</em> and not\n<em>making</em>, you'd rather be a streamer than a YouTuber — and that's fine to know now.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>🧠 The one-word difference: CONSISTENCY</h2>\n<p>Every big channel has the same boring origin story:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Video 1 — nobody watches</li>\n<li>Video 5 — nobody watches</li>\n<li>Video 20 — still small</li>\n<li>Video 40 — one video pops 🚀</li>\n</ol>\n<p>The algorithm doesn't reward talent first. It rewards <strong>reliability</strong>. One video a\nweek for six months beats ten videos in one week and then silence.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>💬 MrBeast uploaded for <strong>six years</strong> before anything big happened.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr />\n<h2>🧠 The niche rule: narrow beats broad</h2>\n<p>❌ \"I make gaming videos\" — you're competing with 50 million channels.\n✅ \"I make <strong>Rivals</strong> loadout guides\" — you're competing with a few hundred.</p>\n<p>You can widen later. <strong>Narrow first.</strong> Your niche is the cross of things only <em>you</em>\nhave:</p>\n<pre><code>   Rivals (you play it constantly)\n        ╳  K-pop (you know the fandoms)\n        ╳  Your humour\n        =  your channel\n</code></pre>\n<hr />\n<h2>✏️ Your turn (30 seconds)</h2>\n<p>Finish this sentence out loud:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><em>\"My channel is the place where people come to watch ______.\"</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>If you can't fill the blank yet, that's fine — that's Step 2.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>⚡ Quiz</h2>\n<p>Scroll down! ⭐</p>"},{"id":"step-02","label":"2. Plan Your Channel","title":"🗺️ Step 2: Plan Your Channel","group":"The 20 Minutes","groupEmoji":"⏱️","emoji":"🗺️","blurb":"Niche, name, and your first 10 videos.","kind":"doc","quiz":{"title":"Step 2 — Plan Your Channel","questions":[{"q":"Why write 10 video ideas BEFORE video 1?","options":["It's homework","Channels die when video 2 has no idea","YouTube requires it","It fills the description"],"answer":1,"why":"The 'what do I make next?' gap is what kills most channels."},{"q":"What is the 'One Viewer' trick?","options":["Make videos for one specific person with one problem","Get one friend to subscribe","Only have one viewer","Make one video"],"answer":0,"why":"Videos made 'for everyone' are watched by no one."},{"q":"Which channel name is best?","options":["xX_jeffrey_293","JeffreyPlays","Untitled Channel","RivalsKing8838"],"answer":1,"why":"Easy to say and spell, works everywhere, not locked to one game."},{"q":"Why is 'my gameplay #4' a bad video idea?","options":["It's too short","It has no clear promise — nobody clicks it","Gameplay is banned","It's too long"],"answer":1,"why":"Every video needs a clear promise in the title, not a number."}]},"html":"<p><strong>⏱️ 2:00 → 6:00 (4 minutes)</strong></p>\n<h2>🎯 Goal</h2>\n<p>Leave this page with a <strong>niche</strong>, a <strong>name</strong>, and <strong>10 video ideas</strong>. Written down.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>🧠 1. Pick your niche (2 options is fine)</h2>\n<p>For you, two strong candidates:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Niche</th>\n<th>Why it works</th>\n<th>Your angle</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Rivals / Roblox</strong> 🎮</td>\n<td>You know it cold; players search for guides</td>\n<td>Loadouts, tips, updates, tier lists</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>K-pop reactions</strong> 🎤</td>\n<td>Fandoms rewatch and share everything</td>\n<td>First-time reactions, rankings, news</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>💡 Best move for a 12-year-old gamer: <strong>start with Rivals.</strong> Gaming is safer (no\nface needed), and guides get searched forever. Keep K-pop as channel #2 later — or\nmix in \"gamer reacts to K-pop\" as your spice.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>🧠 2. Name your channel</h2>\n<p>Rules for a good name:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>✅ Easy to <strong>say</strong> and <strong>spell</strong></li>\n<li>✅ Works as a <strong>username</strong> (YouTube, Roblox, Discord — same everywhere)</li>\n<li>✅ Not locked to one game (\"RivalsKing\" hurts if you switch games)</li>\n<li>❌ No numbers or underscores if you can avoid it (<code>JeffreyPlays</code> &gt; <code>xX_jeffrey_293</code>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Test:</strong> say it out loud. Could a friend find it by hearing it once?</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>🧠 3. The First 10 list</h2>\n<p>Write <strong>10 video ideas now</strong>, before you make video 1. Channels die because video 2\nhas no idea. Your first 10 for a Rivals channel:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Rivals in 60 seconds (complete beginner guide)</li>\n<li>Top 5 weapons ranked</li>\n<li>Best loadout for [your main]</li>\n<li>5 mistakes every new player makes</li>\n<li>Update breakdown — what changed</li>\n<li>I used the <em>worst</em> weapon for a whole match</li>\n<li>Pro settings copy-paste</li>\n<li>Ranking every map</li>\n<li>Free-to-play vs paying — honest take</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A — ask me anything about Rivals</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Notice: every one has a <strong>clear promise</strong>. Not \"my gameplay #4\" — nobody clicks that.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>🧠 4. The One Viewer trick 🎯</h2>\n<p>Before filming, write one sentence:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><em>\"This video is for the Rivals player who keeps dying in the first 30 seconds.\"</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>One viewer, one problem. Videos made \"for everyone\" are watched by no one.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>✏️ Your turn (2 minutes)</h2>\n<p>Write your: <strong>niche → name → first 3 video ideas.</strong> Seriously, on paper. Step 3\nuses them.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>⚡ Quiz</h2>\n<p>Scroll down! ⭐</p>"},{"id":"step-03","label":"3. Make Your First Video","title":"🎬 Step 3: Make Your First Video","group":"The 20 Minutes","groupEmoji":"⏱️","emoji":"🎬","blurb":"The script formula: hook, body, payoff.","kind":"doc","quiz":{"title":"Step 3 — Make Your First Video","questions":[{"q":"What must the first 8-15 seconds do?","options":["Play the channel intro music","Welcome everyone to the channel","Deliver the hook — who it's for and what they get","Say nothing while gameplay plays"],"answer":2,"why":"Viewers decide in ~8 seconds. 'Hey guys welcome back' loses them."},{"q":"What is retention?","options":["The % of the video people actually watch","How many videos you keep","Your subscriber count","How long your channel lasts"],"answer":0,"why":"Retention is the biggest ranking signal. Keep people watching."},{"q":"You're 12 and don't want to show your face. Best option?","options":["Wait until you're older","Voice + gameplay, no face","Text and music only","Wear a mask"],"answer":1,"why":"Voice + gameplay is perfect for gaming — connection without exposure."},{"q":"What matters more than a fancy camera?","options":["Clear audio and tight editing","A gaming chair","RGB lights","A 4K webcam"],"answer":0,"why":"Clear audio and tight editing. The camera barely matters."}]},"html":"<p><strong>⏱️ 6:00 → 12:00 (6 minutes)</strong></p>\n<h2>🎯 Goal</h2>\n<p>Learn the <strong>script formula</strong> that keeps people watching — and the free tools that\nmake it look good.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>🧠 The 3-part script formula</h2>\n<p>Every good video, from 60 seconds to 20 minutes, is the same shape:</p>\n<h3>1. HOOK (0–15 sec) — earn the click</h3>\n<p>Tell them exactly what they get:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><em>\"This is the loadout that got me from Bronze to Diamond — and the third weapon\nalmost nobody uses.\"</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>❌ Never start with \"Hey guys, welcome back to my channel, today I'm going to…\"\nViewers decide in <strong>8 seconds.</strong> The intro <em>is</em> the video starting.</p>\n<h3>2. BODY — deliver the promise, in order</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>One point at a time</li>\n<li>Show, don't just tell (gameplay on screen while you explain)</li>\n<li>Cut every silence. If a second adds nothing, it goes.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>3. PAYOFF + next step (last 15 sec)</h3>\n<p>Land the promise, then point forward:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><em>\"That's the loadout — drop yours in the comments. Next video: I'm testing the\ngun everyone says is trash.\"</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr />\n<h2>🧠 The retention rule 📉</h2>\n<p><strong>Retention</strong> = the % of your video people watch. It's the biggest ranking signal.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Enemy</th>\n<th>Fix</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Slow intro</td>\n<td>Hook first, branding later</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Rambling</td>\n<td>Script bullet points, not paragraphs</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Dead air</td>\n<td>Cut. Cut. Cut.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>No structure</td>\n<td>\"3 tips\" beats \"some tips\"</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Watch your own video back. <strong>Where did you get bored?</strong> That's where viewers leave.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>🧠 Voice or no voice?</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Voice, no face:</strong> perfect for gaming at 12. Cheap mic is fine; quiet room matters more.</li>\n<li><strong>Face cam:</strong> builds connection — maybe later.</li>\n<li><strong>No voice at all:</strong> possible (text + music) but much harder to grow.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>You don't need a fancy camera. You need clear audio and tight editing.</strong></p>\n<hr />\n<h2>🧠 The free toolkit (it's all you need)</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Job</th>\n<th>Free tool</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Record gameplay</td>\n<td><strong>OBS Studio</strong> (free, standard)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Edit</td>\n<td><strong>CapCut</strong> (easy) or <strong>DaVinci Resolve</strong> (pro)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Thumbnails</td>\n<td><strong>Canva</strong> (use their YouTube templates)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Audio cleanup</td>\n<td>CapCut's built-in \"enhance voice\"</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>💡 <strong>Thumbnail rule:</strong> big face or big object, 3 words max, readable at phone size.\nLook at the Rivals thumbnails that got YOU to click. Copy that energy, not that\ncontent.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>✏️ Your turn (2 minutes)</h2>\n<p>Script video #1 from your Step 2 list — just three blocks:</p>\n<p><strong>HOOK:</strong> ________ <strong>BODY:</strong> 3 bullets <strong>PAYOFF:</strong> ________</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>⚡ Quiz</h2>\n<p>Scroll down! ⭐</p>"},{"id":"step-04","label":"4. Upload Like a Pro","title":"🚀 Step 4: Upload Like a Pro","group":"The 20 Minutes","groupEmoji":"⏱️","emoji":"🚀","blurb":"Titles, thumbnails, CTR and retention.","kind":"doc","quiz":{"title":"Step 4 — Upload Like a Pro","questions":[{"q":"What decides your CTR?","options":["Your title and thumbnail","Your editing software","Your upload speed","Your subscriber count"],"answer":0,"why":"CTR is decided before anyone watches — it's the packaging."},{"q":"What's a good target CTR?","options":["0.5–1%","4–10%","50%","100%"],"answer":1,"why":"4–10% is solid. Below that, fix the thumbnail and title."},{"q":"Why make the thumbnail BEFORE editing?","options":["It's faster","If you can't make a compelling thumbnail, the video isn't compelling","YouTube requires the thumbnail first","Thumbnails cost money"],"answer":1,"why":"The thumbnail is the promise. If it doesn't work, rethink the video."},{"q":"What's the smart play with Shorts?","options":["Only make Shorts","Cut the best 30 seconds of your long video as a Short pointing to it","Never make Shorts","Make Shorts instead of long videos"],"answer":1,"why":"One effort, two products. Shorts for discovery, long videos for the audience."}]},"html":"<p><strong>⏱️ 12:00 → 16:00 (4 minutes)</strong></p>\n<h2>🎯 Goal</h2>\n<p>The video is made. Now the 15% that decides whether anyone sees it: <strong>title,\nthumbnail, timing.</strong></p>\n<hr />\n<h2>🧠 The two numbers that rule everything</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Metric</th>\n<th>Meaning</th>\n<th>Good looks like</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>CTR</strong> (click-through rate)</td>\n<td>% who saw the thumbnail and clicked</td>\n<td>4–10%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Retention</strong></td>\n<td>% of the video actually watched</td>\n<td>40%+</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<ul>\n<li>CTR = your <strong>title + thumbnail</strong> (decided <em>before</em> they watch)</li>\n<li>Retention = your <strong>video quality</strong> (Step 3)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The algorithm doesn't promote \"good videos.\" It promotes videos <strong>people click and\nfinish.</strong> You now control both.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>🧠 Titles: the curiosity formula</h2>\n<p>❌ <code>Rivals gameplay ep 4</code>\n✅ <code>The Loadout Nobody Uses (It's Broken)</code>\n✅ <code>I Played Rivals With Only the Worst Gun</code>\n✅ <code>Rivals in 60 Seconds — Everything You Need</code></p>\n<p><strong>Formula:</strong> <em>[specific thing] + [why I care]</em>. Numbers, stakes, or a twist. Under\n60 characters so it doesn't get cut off.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>🧠 Thumbnails: 3 rules</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Readable at phone size</strong> — most viewers are on phones</li>\n<li><strong>One focal point</strong> — a face, a gun, a result. Not a busy screenshot.</li>\n<li><strong>≤3 words</strong> of text, huge</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Make the thumbnail <strong>before</strong> you edit the video. If you can't make a compelling\nthumbnail, you don't have a compelling video.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>🧠 Description &amp; tags (the 2-minute version)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>First line = repeat the promise</strong> (it shows in search)</li>\n<li>Add: what's in the video, 3–5 relevant search terms naturally</li>\n<li><strong>Tags matter little now</strong> — title and thumbnail matter a lot</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<h2>🧠 Shorts vs long videos</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>Shorts 📱</th>\n<th>Long videos ▶️</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Best for</td>\n<td>Fast growth, discovery</td>\n<td>Building a real audience</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Your move</td>\n<td>Clip your best 30 sec</td>\n<td>Main channel content</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Smart play:</strong> make the long video, cut the best moment into a Short that points\nto it. One effort, two products.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>🧠 Schedule: pick it and keep it</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>One day, one time, every week.</strong> e.g. Saturday 10am HK time (after school\n  hours in Asia <em>and</em> US evening the night before 🌏)</li>\n<li>Consistency trains both the algorithm <em>and</em> your viewers</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<h2>✏️ Your turn (1 minute)</h2>\n<p>Write the <strong>title</strong> and <strong>thumbnail text</strong> for video #1. Three words max on the\nthumbnail.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>⚡ Quiz</h2>\n<p>Scroll down! ⭐</p>"},{"id":"step-05","label":"5. Grow & Stay Safe","title":"📈 Step 5: Grow & Stay Safe","group":"The 20 Minutes","groupEmoji":"⏱️","emoji":"📈","blurb":"The rules that compound - and the rules that protect you.","kind":"doc","quiz":{"title":"Step 5 — Grow & Stay Safe","questions":[{"q":"When should you judge your channel's success?","options":["After video 1","After video 3","After 20 videos","After the first week"],"answer":2,"why":"The 20-video deal: first 10 are practice, 10–20 is where style emerges."},{"q":"What does the YouTube Partner Program require?","options":["100 subscribers","1,000 subs + 4,000 watch hours (or 10M Shorts views), and 13+","1 million views","A sponsorship deal"],"answer":1,"why":"And realistically it's 6–18 months of consistent work away."},{"q":"Which is NEVER okay to share?","options":["Your favourite loadout","Your school, address or daily routine","Your gameplay clips","Your opinion on a weapon"],"answer":1,"why":"Viewers include people you don't want knowing your location or routine."},{"q":"Why should you not read out hate comments on camera?","options":["It's boring","It feeds the trolls and hurts you","The video gets too long","Comments can't be filmed"],"answer":1,"why":"Trolls want the reaction. Block, delete, move on."}]},"html":"<p><strong>⏱️ 16:00 → 20:00 (4 minutes)</strong></p>\n<h2>🎯 Goal</h2>\n<p>The long game: what actually grows a channel — and the rules that keep <em>you</em> safe\nwhile it does.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>🧠 Part 1 — The growth rules that compound</h2>\n<h3>1. The 20-video deal 📅</h3>\n<p>Judge nothing before 20 videos. Your first 10 are practice. Videos 10–20 are where\nyou find your style. Most creators quit at 3 — that's the whole trick: <strong>don't.</strong></p>\n<h3>2. Watch your own analytics 📊</h3>\n<p>After each video, check two numbers: where CTR is low → fix thumbnail; where\nretention drops → fix editing. Every video is a lesson, not a lottery ticket.</p>\n<h3>3. Reply to every comment (early on) 💬</h3>\n<p>Your first 100 viewers are worth more than your next 100,000. A channel with 5\nloyal commenters beats one with 500 silent ones.</p>\n<h3>4. Steal like an artist 🎨</h3>\n<p>Find 5 Rivals/gaming channels you love. For each of their top videos ask: <em>why did\nthis work?</em> Copy the <strong>structure</strong> (hook! payoff!) — never the content.</p>\n<h3>5. Collaborate 🤝</h3>\n<p>Other small creators are colleagues, not competition. Duos and shout-outs are how\nsmall channels grow together.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>🧠 Part 2 — The money truth (honest version)</h2>\n<p>The <strong>YouTube Partner Program</strong> requires:\n- <strong>1,000 subscribers</strong>, and\n- <strong>4,000 public watch hours</strong> in 12 months <strong>or</strong> 10M Shorts views in 90 days\n- You must be <strong>13+</strong> (and payment needs an AdSense account — adults handle this)</p>\n<p>Reality check: that's month 6–18 of consistent work for most. <strong>Don't start for the\nmoney.</strong> Start because you'd make videos anyway — that's the only motivation that\nsurvives to video 50, where the money actually starts.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>⚠️ Part 3 — Safety rules for a 12-year-old creator (non-negotiable)</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Rule</th>\n<th>Why</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Your parents know and approve your channel</strong></td>\n<td>Age rules, protection, and honestly better videos</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Never share</strong>: real full name, school, address, phone, daily routines</td>\n<td>Viewers include people you don't want knowing that</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>No meetups</strong> with viewers, ever, without a parent</td>\n<td>People online are not always who they say</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Comments on = moderated</strong></td>\n<td>Delete/block anything weird, immediately</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Don't read out hate comments on camera</strong></td>\n<td>Feeds the trolls; hurts you</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>It's \"made for kids\" or it isn't</strong> — set it honestly</td>\n<td>COPPA rules; wrong settings kill your comments and notifications</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Screen-time honesty</strong> 🎮</td>\n<td>School first. Burnout kills more channels than the algorithm</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<blockquote>\n<p>💬 The creators who last treat it like a <strong>craft</strong>. The ones who flame out treat\nit like a slot machine.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr />\n<h2>🎓 You've finished Bootcamp</h2>\n<p>You now know more about the <em>job</em> of YouTube than most people who \"want to be a\nYouTuber.\" The only thing left is the hard part:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Make video one. This month.</h2>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Use the <strong>Script Template</strong> and <strong>Rivals Example</strong> pages when you plan it. 🫡</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>⚡ Quiz</h2>\n<p>Scroll down! ⭐</p>"},{"id":"example","label":"Rivals Example","title":"🎮 Worked Example: \"JF Rivals Lab\"","group":"Reference","groupEmoji":"🗂️","emoji":"🎮","blurb":"The whole course applied to a Rivals channel, start to finish.","kind":"doc","quiz":null,"html":"<p>Here's the whole course applied to a <strong>Rivals channel</strong>, start to finish — steal this structure.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>📋 The channel plan</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Decision</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Niche</strong></td>\n<td>Rivals guides + tier lists (Roblox gaming)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>One viewer</strong></td>\n<td>\"The Rivals player stuck in Bronze who wants better aim\"</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Name</strong></td>\n<td>Something clean, ownable, spellable — e.g. <em>JF Rivals Lab</em></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Format</strong></td>\n<td>4–8 min videos, voice + gameplay, no face</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Schedule</strong></td>\n<td>Every Saturday, 10am HK time</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h2>🎬 Video #1, fully scripted</h2>\n<p><strong>Title:</strong> <code>Rivals in 5 Minutes — The Complete Beginner Guide</code>\n<strong>Thumbnail:</strong> shocked face + \"IN 5 MIN\" (3 words)\n<strong>Hook (0:00–0:12):</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><em>\"If you're losing your first fight every match, this is the video for you.\nFive minutes, everything that matters: movement, your first weapon, and the one\nsetting almost nobody changes.\"</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Body (bullets on your screen while playing):</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Movement first</strong> — strafe while shooting; standing still = dying</li>\n<li><strong>The starter weapon that wins fights</strong> — show 3 clips of it working</li>\n<li><strong>The setting</strong> — sensitivity/crosshair change, show before/after</li>\n<li><strong>Recap</strong> — the 3 things, one sentence each</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Payoff (last 15 sec):</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><em>\"Movement, weapon, settings — that's the whole beginner game. Next Saturday:\nI'm ranking every weapon from trash to broken. Sub so you don't miss it.\"</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr />\n<h2>📅 The first month, realistically</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Week</th>\n<th>Video</th>\n<th>Why this one</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>Beginner guide</td>\n<td>Evergreen; new players search it forever</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>Weapon tier list</td>\n<td>Clickable, arguable, comment fuel</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>\"The loadout nobody uses\"</td>\n<td>Curiosity title, shows your knowledge</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>Update breakdown</td>\n<td>Timely; rides the update search wave</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Analytics ritual after each upload (5 min):</strong> CTR low → new thumbnail. Big drop\nat 0:30 → hook too slow. Nobody's fault. Just data.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>🎤 Where the K-pop fits</h2>\n<p>Once the channel moves, sprinkle what makes it <em>yours</em>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Background music vibes (royalty-free only — see Grown-Ups note!)</li>\n<li>\"Rivals but every kill plays a K-pop chorus\" type formats</li>\n<li>A second channel later, or community posts</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Your taste is your differentiation.</strong> Ten thousand people can make a Rivals\nguide. Only you make <em>yours</em>.</p>"},{"id":"script","label":"Script Template","title":"✍️ Script Template","group":"Reference","groupEmoji":"🗂️","emoji":"✏️","blurb":"Copy this before every video.","kind":"doc","quiz":null,"html":"<p>Copy this into a doc before every video. Fill the boxes, film, done.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>📋 Pre-flight</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>One viewer:</strong> <em>This video is for the Rivals player who ______</em></li>\n<li><strong>Promise:</strong> After watching, they can ______</li>\n<li><strong>Thumbnail text (≤3 words):</strong> ______</li>\n<li><strong>Title (≤60 chars):</strong> ______</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<h2>🎬 The script</h2>\n<h3>HOOK (0:00–0:12) — write it word for word</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><em>\"______________________________.\"</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>(Must contain: who it's for + what they get. No \"hey guys welcome back\".)</p>\n<h3>BODY — max 3–4 points, one line each</h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Point 1:</strong> ______ <em>(show: gameplay clip of ___)</em></li>\n<li><strong>Point 2:</strong> ______ <em>(show: ___)</em></li>\n<li><strong>Point 3:</strong> ______ <em>(show: ___)</em></li>\n</ol>\n<h3>PAYOFF (last 15 sec) — write it word for word</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><em>\"______________________________.\"</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>(Must contain: the promise kept + where to go next.)</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>✂️ Edit checklist</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[ ] Hook lands in the <strong>first 8 seconds</strong></li>\n<li>[ ] Every silence cut</li>\n<li>[ ] Gameplay visible during every explanation</li>\n<li>[ ] Music quiet under voice</li>\n<li>[ ] Watched it back once, <strong>got bored nowhere</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<h2>📤 Upload checklist</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[ ] Title ≤ 60 chars, has a number/stakes/twist</li>\n<li>[ ] Thumbnail readable at phone size, 1 focal point</li>\n<li>[ ] First line of description = the promise</li>\n<li>[ ] \"Made for kids\" set correctly</li>\n<li>[ ] Scheduled for the regular slot</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"toolkit","label":"Free Toolkit","title":"🧰 The Free Toolkit","group":"Reference","groupEmoji":"🗂️","emoji":"🧰","blurb":"OBS, CapCut, Canva - everything you need, $0.","kind":"doc","quiz":null,"html":"<p>Everything below is free and standard among creators. You need nothing else to start.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>🎥 Recording</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Tool</th>\n<th>Use</th>\n<th>Notes</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>OBS Studio</strong></td>\n<td>Gameplay + voice</td>\n<td>The industry standard; works on any PC</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Roblox's own recorder</strong></td>\n<td>Quick clips</td>\n<td>Fine for Shorts; OBS for real videos</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Phone voice memo</strong></td>\n<td>Backup audio</td>\n<td>Always record a spare track</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>OBS settings that matter:</strong> 1080p, 30fps (60 if your PC can), and record a\n<strong>test clip first.</strong> Nothing hurts like a perfect take that didn't save.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>✂️ Editing</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Tool</th>\n<th>Best for</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>CapCut</strong></td>\n<td>Starting out — cuts, music, captions, all easy</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>DaVinci Resolve</strong></td>\n<td>When you outgrow CapCut — pro colour and audio</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Rule: <strong>learn 5 features deeply</strong> (cut, text, music, zoom, speed) instead of 50\nbadly. Fancy transitions aren't why anyone subscribes.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>🖼️ Thumbnails</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Tool</th>\n<th>Use</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Canva</strong></td>\n<td>YouTube thumbnail templates → swap text and image</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Screenshot from your video</strong></td>\n<td>Better than stock — it's authentic</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>The 3-second test:</strong> open your thumbnail on a phone, look away, look back. Do you\nunderstand the video in 3 seconds?</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>📊 After upload</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Tool</th>\n<th>Use</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>YouTube Studio</strong> (app or web)</td>\n<td>CTR, retention, comments</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>The 'top search terms' panel</strong></td>\n<td>What people actually type — future video ideas</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h2>💰 Total cost of entry: $0</h2>\n<p>The barrier was never money. It's the 20 videos.</p>"},{"id":"grownups","label":"For Grown-Ups","title":"🧑‍🏫 For Grown-Ups","group":"Reference","groupEmoji":"🗂️","emoji":"🧑‍🏫","blurb":"Account rules, safety settings, copyright, realistic expectations.","kind":"doc","quiz":null,"html":"<p>Jeffrey's course is finished — this page is for you. Five minutes, honest, no hype.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>📜 The account rules (the important bit)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>YouTube requires users to be 13+ to have their own account.</strong> At 12, the\n  correct setup is a <strong>parent-managed account</strong> (Google Family Link), with you\n  holding the settings.</li>\n<li><strong>COPPA:</strong> every upload must declare whether content is \"made for kids.\"\n  Mislabelling has real penalties — set it honestly per video. \"Made for kids\"\n  disables comments and notifications; gaming content for teens is normally <strong>not</strong>\n  marked as made-for-kids.</li>\n<li><strong>Monetisation</strong> needs 1,000 subs + 4,000 watch hours (or 10M Shorts views/90\n  days), <strong>13+</strong>, and an adult-managed AdSense account. Realistically 6–18 months\n  away — treat any money talk as motivation, not a plan.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<h2>🛡️ Safety settings worth agreeing on together</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[ ] Parents are <strong>administrators</strong> on the channel account</li>\n<li>[ ] Comments set to <strong>hold potentially inappropriate for review</strong></li>\n<li>[ ] No real name, school, address, or routine in videos or descriptions</li>\n<li>[ ] No in-person meetups with viewers, ever, without a parent</li>\n<li>[ ] DMs from strangers stay unanswered; anything odd → tell a parent, screenshot, block</li>\n<li>[ ] A weekly time budget for making videos that <strong>school wins</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<h2>⚖️ Copyright, in one paragraph</h2>\n<p>Game footage is generally fine under publisher-friendly policies (Roblox explicitly\nallows monetised videos). <strong>Music is the trap:</strong> K-pop tracks will get videos\nclaimed, muted or blocked. The habit to build now: <strong>royalty-free music only</strong>\n(CapCut's library, YouTube Audio Library). Reaction videos should use short clips\nwith real commentary, not full songs. This one habit prevents most channel strikes.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>🎯 What success looks like at 12</h2>\n<p>The realistic best case isn't money — it's a <strong>portfolio</strong>: a kid who can script,\nedit, present, analyse data, and handle criticism. Those are career skills with or\nwithout YouTube. The realistic worst case is burnout or an unmoderated comment\nsection — both prevented by the checkboxes above.</p>\n<p><strong>The single most protective rule:</strong> he tells you about the weird comment before he\nreplies to it. Keep that channel open and everything else is manageable.</p>"}]};
